    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0112" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/181<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >1/10</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hinkle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad
                                Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-30T15:00:00-05:00">May 30, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>83. Department’s telegram No. 61, May 29, noon [<hi rendition="#italic">3
                        p.m.</hi>]<anchor n="42" xml:id="d119-f1"/> The President<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d119-f2"/> said that his Government was entirely in accord with the
                    Department’s suggestion and that it would be ready to put into operation at any
                    time. The President added that General Trujillo authorized him to offer any type
                    of cooperation whatsoever.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hinkle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
